Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:10:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify rejected oversized signing-provider scripts

Retain the non-dropping Error diagnostic and its original text/limit while
recording only unsigned size metadata. Never include redeem-script or key
bytes. Keep rejection, locking and mapScripts insertion unchanged.

Add a focused public AddCScript test: one byte above the existing limit
is rejected and absent from the store, the exact limit remains accepted
and retrievable, and the actual rejection JSON has numeric limit metadata,
Error severity and no script/truncation field. No node or network traffic.

Shared eCash signing-provider owner. Source-only event lint/diff checks
pass; new native case NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. No conversion changes current
script validity or V2 VM behavior. Sealed381/current intake is unchanged.

